    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28448" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕlanthĭum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-on</span></b> ), ii,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελάνθιον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the plant</i> gith,
				<i>cultivated fennel-flower</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gith e Graecis alii melanthion, alii
					melaspermon, vocant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					20, 17, 71, § 182</span></i>
			; Col. poët. 10, 245; also <i>chamomile</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 22, 21, 26, §
			53</span></i>.—Called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕlanthum</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Ser. Samm.
				30</span></i>.</div>
